12. Suggested Project Folder Structure
project-name/ | README.md | architecture.md | app/ | frontend/ | data/ | evals/ | docs/ | tests/ | requirements.txt | .env.example | SECURITY.md
13. Final Advice
Do not learn everything only theoretically. Use this loop: Learn concept → Build mini project → Write README → Add screenshot → Publish → Explain architecture → Improve.
Your advantage is already clear: you are not starting from zero. You already have enterprise GenAI exposure. Now convert that experience into visible public proof through GitHub, portfolio, LinkedIn, and resume-ready projects.
